{
  name: "cheriot_mem_sys"
  // The planned functional checks of the CHERIoT memory subsystem FPV environment. A
  // testpoint lists its requirements under `features`; each is defined, with its
  // sources and the reason its checks prove it, in cheriot_mem_sys_fpv_requirements.hjson. A
  // check row may also decide a requirement of another testpoint, which then says so.
  testpoints: [
    {
      name: tf_forward
      desc: '''Every core access reaches the host port once, unchanged, in the cycle the core presents it.
Its answer carries the host answer's fields when its last part arrives.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | forwarded unchanged: `assert_TfForward_ForwardedUnchanged` | forward | [REQ_TF_01b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_01b), [REQ_TF_01e](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_01e), [REQ_TF_01f](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_01f), [REQ_TF_01g](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_01g), [REQ_TF_01h](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_01h), [REQ_TF_01i](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_01i), [REQ_TF_01j](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_01j), [REQ_TF_16a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_16a), [REQ_WTRC_13a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_13a), [REQ_WTRC_13b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_13b), [REQ_TBRE_39](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_39) |
            | no extra host request: `assert_TfForward_NoExtraHostRequest` | backward | [REQ_TF_01d](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_01d), [REQ_TF_01c](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_01c) |
            | accepted after forwarded: `assert_TfForward_AcceptedAfterForwarded` | forward | [REQ_TF_01a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_01a) |
            | answer has host fields: `assert_TfForward_AnswerHasHostFields` | forward | [REQ_TF_07a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_07a), [REQ_TF_07b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_07b), [REQ_TF_07c](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_07c), [REQ_TF_07d](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_07d), [REQ_TF_07e](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_07e), [REQ_TF_07f](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_07f) |
            | answer on last part: `assert_TfForward_AnswerOnLastPart` | forward | [REQ_TF_16b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_16b), [REQ_WTRC_13b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_13b) |

            18 [requirements](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#tag-filter) belong to this testpoint.
            The table also names requirements of other testpoints that its checks help decide.'''
      stage: V1
      priority: "1"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_TF_01a", "REQ_TF_01d", "REQ_TF_01c", "REQ_TF_01b", "REQ_TF_01e", "REQ_TF_01f", "REQ_TF_01g", "REQ_TF_01h", "REQ_TF_01i", "REQ_TF_01j", "REQ_TF_07a", "REQ_TF_07b", "REQ_TF_07c", "REQ_TF_07d", "REQ_TF_07e", "REQ_TF_07f", "REQ_TF_16a", "REQ_TF_16b"]
    }
    {
      name: tf_lookup
      desc: '''A request that needs a lookup issues exactly one meta request, in the same cycle.
Every other request issues none.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | lookup in same cycle: `assert_TfLookup_LookupInSameCycle` | forward | [REQ_TF_02a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_02a), [REQ_TF_03a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_03a), [REQ_TF_16c](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_16c), [REQ_TAG_02](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_02), [REQ_TAG_03](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_03), [REQ_TBRE_39](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_39) |
            | no unneeded lookup: `assert_TfLookup_NoUnneededLookup` | backward | [REQ_TF_02b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_02b), [REQ_TF_03b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_03b), [REQ_TF_04a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_04a), [REQ_TF_04b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_04b), [REQ_WTRC_06b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_06b), [REQ_WTRC_08b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_08b), [REQ_TAG_02](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_02), [REQ_TAG_03](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_03), [REQ_ALT_04](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_alt_04) |
            | lookup carries valid integrity: `assert_TfLookup_LookupCarriesValidIntegrity` | forward | [REQ_TF_17](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_17) |

            8 [requirements](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#tag-filter) belong to this testpoint.
            The table also names requirements of other testpoints that its checks help decide.'''
      stage: V1
      priority: "1"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_TF_02a", "REQ_TF_02b", "REQ_TF_03a", "REQ_TF_03b", "REQ_TF_04a", "REQ_TF_04b", "REQ_TF_16c", "REQ_TF_17"]
    }
    {
      name: tf_meta_request
      desc: '''Each meta request names the right tag word and bit, and a write asks for the tag its sideband carries.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | tag word and bit: `assert_TfMetaRequest_TagWordAndBit` | forward | [REQ_TF_05a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_05a), [REQ_TF_05b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_05b), [REQ_TAG_01](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_01), [REQ_TAG_02](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_02), [REQ_TAG_03](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_03), [REQ_TAG_04](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_04), [REQ_ALT_04](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_alt_04) |
            | write carries its tag: `assert_TfMetaRequest_WriteCarriesItsTag` | forward | [REQ_TF_06a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_06a), [REQ_TF_06b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_06b), [REQ_TF_06c](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_06c), [REQ_TAG_02](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_02), [REQ_TAG_03](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_03) |
            | Get only for a read: `assert_TfMetaRequest_GetOnlyForARead` | forward | [REQ_TF_06a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_06a), [REQ_TF_06b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_06b), [REQ_TF_06c](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_06c), [REQ_TAG_02](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_02), [REQ_TAG_03](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_03) |

            5 [requirements](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#tag-filter) belong to this testpoint.
            The table also names requirements of other testpoints that its checks help decide.'''
      stage: V1
      priority: "1"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_TF_05a", "REQ_TF_05b", "REQ_TF_06a", "REQ_TF_06b", "REQ_TF_06c"]
    }
    {
      name: tf_sticky_tag
      desc: '''The tag returned with each answer is the meta tag for W0 of a capability load, the captured tag for the W1 after it, and 0 for every other answer.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | answer tag follows rule: `assert_TfStickyTag_AnswerTagFollowsRule` | forward | [REQ_TF_08](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_08), [REQ_TF_09](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_09), [REQ_TF_10](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_10), [REQ_TF_11a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_11a), [REQ_TF_11b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_11b), [REQ_TF_11c](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_11c), [REQ_TF_11d](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_11d), [REQ_TF_18a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_18a), [REQ_TAG_01](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_01) |
            | untagged answer carries MuBi4False: `assert_TfStickyTag_UntaggedAnswerCarriesMuBi4False` | forward | [REQ_TF_18b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_18b) |

            9 [requirements](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#tag-filter) belong to this testpoint.
            The table also names requirements of other testpoints that its checks help decide.'''
      stage: V1
      priority: "1"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_TF_08", "REQ_TF_09", "REQ_TF_10", "REQ_TF_11a", "REQ_TF_11b", "REQ_TF_11c", "REQ_TF_11d", "REQ_TF_18a", "REQ_TF_18b"]
    }
    {
      name: tf_errors
      desc: '''An error in the host or the meta answer reaches the core, no error is invented, and a merged error keeps the integrity valid or broken as it was.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | error when a part has one: `assert_TfErrors_ErrorWhenAPartHasOne` | forward | [REQ_TF_12a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_12a), [REQ_TF_12c](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_12c) |
            | no error without a cause: `assert_TfErrors_NoErrorWithoutACause` | backward | [REQ_TF_12b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_12b) |
            | merged error keeps integrity: `assert_TfErrors_MergedErrorKeepsIntegrity` | forward | [REQ_TF_13a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_13a), [REQ_TF_13b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_13b) |

            5 [requirements](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#tag-filter) belong to this testpoint.'''
      stage: V2S
      priority: "2"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_TF_12a", "REQ_TF_12c", "REQ_TF_12b", "REQ_TF_13a", "REQ_TF_13b"]
    }
    {
      name: tf_flow
      desc: '''Meta answers are always taken, and every request is accepted and answered exactly once.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | meta answer taken: `assert_TfFlow_MetaAnswerTaken` | safety | [REQ_TF_14](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_14), [REQ_TAG_09](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_09) |
            | no extra answer: `assert_TfFlow_NoExtraAnswer` | backward | [REQ_TF_15c](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_15c), [REQ_WTRC_05a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_05a) |
            | request eventually accepted: `assert_TfFlow_RequestEventuallyAccepted` | liveness | [REQ_TF_15a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_15a), [REQ_TAG_09](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_09) |
            | request eventually answered: `assert_TfFlow_RequestEventuallyAnswered` | liveness | [REQ_TF_15b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tf_15b), [REQ_WTRC_05a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_05a), [REQ_TAG_09](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_09) |

            4 [requirements](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#tag-filter) belong to this testpoint.
            The table also names requirements of other testpoints that its checks help decide.'''
      stage: V2
      priority: "2"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_TF_14", "REQ_TF_15a", "REQ_TF_15b", "REQ_TF_15c"]
    }
    {
      name: wtrc_store
      desc: '''A capability store to the NVM goes out as a `Get`, makes no lookup, and each word receives one untagged `AccessAck`.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | sent as a full-word Get: `assert_WtrcStore_SentAsAFullWordGet` | forward | [REQ_WTRC_01](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_01) |
            | Get has valid command integrity: `assert_WtrcStore_GetHasValidCommandIntegrity` | forward | [REQ_WTRC_02](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_02) |
            | no lookup for a capability store: `assert_WtrcStore_NoLookupForACapabilityStore` | backward | [REQ_WTRC_03a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_03a), [REQ_WTRC_03b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_03b) |
            | untagged AccessAck answer: `assert_WtrcStore_UntaggedAccessAckAnswer` | forward | [REQ_WTRC_05b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_05b), [REQ_WTRC_05c](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_05c), [REQ_WTRC_05d](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_05d), [REQ_WTRC_05e](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_05e) |

            11 [requirements](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#wtrc) belong to this testpoint.'''
      stage: V2
      priority: "2"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_WTRC_01", "REQ_WTRC_02", "REQ_WTRC_03a", "REQ_WTRC_03b", "REQ_WTRC_05a", "REQ_WTRC_05b", "REQ_WTRC_05c", "REQ_WTRC_05d", "REQ_WTRC_05e", "REQ_WTRC_13a", "REQ_WTRC_13b"]
    }
    {
      name: wtrc_compare
      desc: '''The tag is set only when both words match the NVM, after W1's NVM answer and ahead of any later lookup.
A mismatch gives an error and no alert.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | W0 error on mismatch: `assert_WtrcCompare_W0ErrorOnMismatch` | both | [REQ_WTRC_04a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_04a), [REQ_WTRC_04b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_04b) |
            | only the owed tag write: `assert_WtrcCompare_OnlyTheOwedTagWrite` | forward | [REQ_WTRC_06a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_06a), [REQ_WTRC_06b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_06b), [REQ_WTRC_06c](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_06c) |
            | W1 answered after tag write: `assert_WtrcCompare_W1AnsweredAfterTagWrite` | forward | [REQ_WTRC_06a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_06a), [REQ_WTRC_07a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_07a), [REQ_WTRC_07b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_07b) |
            | W1 error on mismatch: `assert_WtrcCompare_W1ErrorOnMismatch` | forward | [REQ_WTRC_08a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_08a), [REQ_WTRC_08b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_08b) |
            | no alert without a cause: `assert_WtrcCompare_NoAlertWithoutACause` | backward | [REQ_WTRC_09](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_09) |
            | answer after NVM answer: `assert_WtrcCompare_AnswerAfterNvmAnswer` | backward | [REQ_WTRC_04a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_04a) |

            10 [requirements](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#wtrc) belong to this testpoint.'''
      stage: V2
      priority: "2"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_WTRC_04a", "REQ_WTRC_04b", "REQ_WTRC_06a", "REQ_WTRC_06b", "REQ_WTRC_06c", "REQ_WTRC_07a", "REQ_WTRC_07b", "REQ_WTRC_08a", "REQ_WTRC_08b", "REQ_WTRC_09"]
    }
    {
      name: wtrc_faults
      desc: '''A word of a capability store that has a bad integrity code, is partial or is out of sequence is answered with an error, writes no tag and raises the fatal alert.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | faulty word answered with error: `assert_WtrcFaults_FaultyWordAnsweredWithError` | forward | [REQ_WTRC_10a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_10a) |
            | faulty word raises alert: `assert_WtrcFaults_FaultyWordRaisesAlert` | liveness | [REQ_WTRC_11](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_11) |
            | other request out of sequence raises alert: `assert_WtrcFaults_OtherRequestOutOfSequenceRaisesAlert` | liveness | [REQ_WTRC_12](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_12) |
            | other answer passes unchanged: `assert_WtrcFaults_OtherAnswerPassesUnchanged` | forward | [REQ_WTRC_14a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_14a) |
            | answer goes to its own access: `assert_WtrcFaults_AnswerGoesToItsOwnAccess` | forward | [REQ_WTRC_14b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_14b) |
            | matched store after fault sets tag: `assert_WtrcFaults_MatchedStoreAfterFaultSetsTag` | forward | [REQ_WTRC_15](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_15) |
            | tag write only for matched pair: `assert_WtrcFaults_TagWriteOnlyForMatchedPair` | backward | [REQ_WTRC_10b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_10b), [REQ_WTRC_16](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_16) |
            | store W1 answered: `assert_WtrcFaults_StoreW1Answered` | liveness | [REQ_WTRC_15](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_15), [REQ_WTRC_17](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_17) |
            | unmatched store after fault errors: `assert_WtrcFaults_UnmatchedStoreAfterFaultErrors` | forward | [REQ_WTRC_17](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_wtrc_17) |

            9 [requirements](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#wtrc) belong to this testpoint.'''
      stage: V2S
      priority: "2"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_WTRC_10a", "REQ_WTRC_10b", "REQ_WTRC_11", "REQ_WTRC_12", "REQ_WTRC_14a", "REQ_WTRC_14b", "REQ_WTRC_15", "REQ_WTRC_17", "REQ_WTRC_16"]
    }
    {
      name: arb_forward
      desc: '''Each request leaves the arbiter once, unchanged, with its own tag and bit select and its input number added to the source ID.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | keeps its own sideband: `assert_ArbForward_KeepsItsOwnSideband` | forward | [REQ_ARB_01a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_01a), [REQ_ARB_03a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_03a), [REQ_ARB_03b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_03b), [REQ_ARB_03c](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_03c), [REQ_ARB_03d](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_03d), [REQ_ARB_03e](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_03e), [REQ_ARB_03f](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_03f), [REQ_ARB_04a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_04a), [REQ_ARB_04b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_04b), [REQ_ARB_06](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_06), [REQ_TAG_01](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_01), [REQ_TAG_02](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_02), [REQ_TAG_03](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_03), [REQ_TAG_04](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_04), [REQ_TBRE_38](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_38) |
            | from the named input: `assert_ArbForward_FromTheNamedInput` | backward | [REQ_ARB_01b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_01b), [REQ_ARB_02](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_02), [REQ_TAG_01](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_01), [REQ_TAG_02](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_02), [REQ_TAG_03](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_03), [REQ_TBRE_38](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_38) |
            | core request unchanged: `assert_ArbForward_CoreRequestUnchanged` | forward | [REQ_ARB_11](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_11), [REQ_TAG_01](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_01), [REQ_TAG_02](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_02), [REQ_TAG_03](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_03), [REQ_TAG_04](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_04) |

            12 [requirements](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#21-tag-arbiter) belong to this testpoint.
            The table also names requirements of other testpoints that its checks help decide.'''
      stage: V1
      priority: "2"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_ARB_01a", "REQ_ARB_01b", "REQ_ARB_02", "REQ_ARB_03a", "REQ_ARB_03b", "REQ_ARB_03c", "REQ_ARB_03d", "REQ_ARB_03e", "REQ_ARB_03f", "REQ_ARB_04a", "REQ_ARB_04b", "REQ_ARB_11"]
    }
    {
      name: arb_return
      desc: '''Each answer goes back only to the input that asked, with its source ID restored and every other field unchanged.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | answer to its input: `assert_ArbReturn_AnswerToItsInput` | backward | [REQ_ARB_05b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_05b), [REQ_TAG_01](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_01) |
            | taken with its input: `assert_ArbReturn_TakenWithItsInput` | both | [REQ_ARB_05a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_05a), [REQ_TAG_01](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_01) |
            | source shifted back: `assert_ArbReturn_SourceShiftedBack` | forward | [REQ_ARB_06](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_06) |
            | fields unchanged: `assert_ArbReturn_FieldsUnchanged` | forward | [REQ_ARB_07a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_07a), [REQ_ARB_07b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_07b), [REQ_ARB_07c](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_07c), [REQ_ARB_07d](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_07d), [REQ_ARB_07e](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_07e), [REQ_ARB_07f](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_07f), [REQ_TAG_01](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tag_01) |

            9 [requirements](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#21-tag-arbiter) belong to this testpoint.
            The table also names requirements of other testpoints that its checks help decide.'''
      stage: V1
      priority: "2"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_ARB_05a", "REQ_ARB_05b", "REQ_ARB_06", "REQ_ARB_07a", "REQ_ARB_07b", "REQ_ARB_07c", "REQ_ARB_07d", "REQ_ARB_07e", "REQ_ARB_07f"]
    }
    {
      name: arb_flow
      desc: '''Requests and answers pass in the same cycle, and neither input waits forever.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | alone in same cycle: `assert_ArbFlow_AloneInSameCycle` | forward | [REQ_ARB_09](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_09), [REQ_TBRE_39](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_39) |
            | answer at once: `assert_ArbFlow_AnswerAtOnce` | forward | [REQ_ARB_10](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_arb_10) |
