    {
      name: tbre_intr
      desc: '''`INTR_STATE.tbre_done` is set when a sweep ends or when software writes 1 to `INTR_TEST.tbre_done`, and only then.
The interrupt line `intr_tbre_done_o` follows whether `INTR_STATE.tbre_done` and `INTR_ENABLE.tbre_done` are both set.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | sweep end or test sets: `assert_TbreIntr_SweepEndOrTestSets` | forward | [REQ_TBRE_28](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_28) |
            | set only on end or test: `assert_TbreIntr_SetOnlyOnEndOrTest` | backward | [REQ_TBRE_30](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_30) |
            | line follows state: `assert_TbreIntr_LineFollowsState` | both | [REQ_TBRE_31](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_31) |

            3 [requirements](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#start-status-and-interrupt) belong to this testpoint.'''
      stage: V2
      priority: "2"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_TBRE_28", "REQ_TBRE_30", "REQ_TBRE_31"]
    }
    {
      name: tbre_sweep
      desc: '''A sweep reads exactly the words of the swept capabilities, with full-word `Get` requests that carry the hint and a valid integrity.
At most two reads are outstanding at a time.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | sweep read carries valid integrity: `assert_TbreSweep_SweepReadCarriesValidIntegrity` | forward | [REQ_TBRE_40](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_40) |
            | both words read: `assert_TbreSweep_BothWordsRead` | forward | [REQ_TBRE_13](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_13) |
            | Gets inside sweep: `assert_TbreSweep_GetsInsideSweep` | backward | [REQ_TBRE_14](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_14) |
            | at most two outstanding: `assert_TbreSweep_AtMostTwoOutstanding` | forward | [REQ_TBRE_15a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_15a), [REQ_TBRE_15b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_15b) |
            | Gets carry hint: `assert_TbreSweep_GetsCarryHint` | forward | [REQ_TBRE_16](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_16) |

            6 [requirements](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#sweep) belong to this testpoint.'''
      stage: V2
      priority: "1"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_TBRE_13", "REQ_TBRE_14", "REQ_TBRE_15a", "REQ_TBRE_15b", "REQ_TBRE_16", "REQ_TBRE_40"]
    }
    {
      name: tbre_done
      desc: '''Every sweep ends, provided that the neighbours of the engine answer.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | sweep ends: `assert_TbreDone_SweepEnds` | liveness | [REQ_TBRE_37](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_37) |

            1 [requirement](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#sweep) belongs to this testpoint.'''
      stage: V2
      priority: "2"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_TBRE_37"]
    }
    {
      name: tbre_decision
      desc: '''The engine looks up the revocation bit of a swept capability only when it can be revoked, and it presents a clear exactly for a revoked capability that no core write touched.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | lookup carries valid integrity: `assert_TbreDecision_LookupCarriesValidIntegrity` | forward | [REQ_TBRE_41](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_41) |
            | lookup when needed: `assert_TbreDecision_LookupWhenNeeded` | forward | [REQ_TBRE_17](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_17) |
            | no lookup outside main SRAM: `assert_TbreDecision_NoLookupOutsideMainSram` | backward | [REQ_TBRE_18](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_18) |
            | lookup is bitmap Get: `assert_TbreDecision_LookupIsBitmapGet` | backward | [REQ_TBRE_17](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_17), [REQ_TBRE_18](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_18) |
            | revoked gets cleared: `assert_TbreDecision_RevokedGetsCleared` | forward | [REQ_TBRE_19](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_19), [REQ_TBRE_34a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_34a), [REQ_TBRE_38](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_38) |
            | clear only if revoked: `assert_TbreDecision_ClearOnlyIfRevoked` | backward | [REQ_TBRE_20](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_20) |

            5 [requirements](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#decision-and-clears) belong to this testpoint.
            The table also names requirements of other testpoints that its checks help decide.'''
      stage: V2
      priority: "1"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_TBRE_17", "REQ_TBRE_18", "REQ_TBRE_19", "REQ_TBRE_20", "REQ_TBRE_41"]
    }
    {
      name: tbre_clear
      desc: '''Each clear is one tag write of tag 0 to the tag bit of the capability.
The engine's tag filter follows the tag filter rules.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | clears tracked bit once: `assert_TbreClear_ClearsTrackedBitOnce` | forward | [REQ_TBRE_21a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_21a), [REQ_TBRE_21b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_21b), [REQ_TBRE_21c](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_21c), [REQ_TBRE_21d](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_21d), [REQ_TBRE_21e](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_21e), [REQ_TBRE_38](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_38) |
            | writes tag 0: `assert_TbreClear_WritesTag0` | backward | [REQ_TBRE_21a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_21a), [REQ_TBRE_38](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_38) |
            | tag filter checks hold: `assert_TbreClear_TagFilterChecksHold` | both | [REQ_TBRE_22](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_22), [REQ_ALT_04](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_alt_04) |
            | write answered once: `assert_TbreClear_WriteAnsweredOnce` | forward | [REQ_TBRE_23a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_23a), [REQ_TBRE_23b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_23b), [REQ_TBRE_23c](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_23c), [REQ_TBRE_23d](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_23d) |

            10 [requirements](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#decision-and-clears) belong to this testpoint.
            The table also names requirements of other testpoints that its checks help decide.'''
      stage: V2
      priority: "1"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_TBRE_21a", "REQ_TBRE_21b", "REQ_TBRE_21c", "REQ_TBRE_21d", "REQ_TBRE_21e", "REQ_TBRE_22", "REQ_TBRE_23a", "REQ_TBRE_23b", "REQ_TBRE_23c", "REQ_TBRE_23d"]
    }
    {
      name: tbre_watch
      desc: '''A capability that the core writes keeps its tag.
After a touch in its watch window, the engine presents no clear for it.
A touch between the presentation of the clear and its arrival at the RMW filter turns the clear into a read.
A clear that waits at the RMW filter stays unchanged until the RMW filter accepts it.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | clear only if untouched: `assert_TbreWatch_ClearOnlyIfUntouched` | backward | [REQ_TBRE_24](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_24), [REQ_TBRE_39](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_39) |
            | stale clear becomes read: `assert_TbreWatch_StaleClearBecomesRead` | forward | [REQ_TBRE_25](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_25), [REQ_TBRE_39](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_39) |
            | fresh clear stays write: `assert_TbreWatch_FreshClearStaysWrite` | forward | [REQ_TBRE_26](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_26), [REQ_TBRE_38](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_38) |
            | clear held unchanged: `assert_TbreWatch_ClearHeldUnchanged` | stable | [REQ_TBRE_27a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_27a), [REQ_TBRE_27b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_27b), [REQ_TBRE_39](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_39) |

            5 [requirements](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#core-write-watch) belong to this testpoint.
            The table also names requirements of other testpoints that its checks help decide.'''
      stage: V2
      priority: "2"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_TBRE_24", "REQ_TBRE_25", "REQ_TBRE_26", "REQ_TBRE_27a", "REQ_TBRE_27b"]
    }
    {
      name: tbre_errors
      desc: '''An error that the engine meets in a sweep sets `sweep_err`, and every such error except an error response to a read also raises `fatal_fault`.
A failed bitmap lookup counts the capability as revoked.

            | Check, and its planned assertion | Kind | Requirements |
            |---|---|---|
            | read error, no clear: `assert_TbreErrors_ReadErrorNoClear` | forward | [REQ_TBRE_32a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_32a) |
            | cause sets sweep error: `assert_TbreErrors_CauseSetsSweepError` | forward | [REQ_TBRE_32b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_32b), [REQ_TBRE_33a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_33a), [REQ_TBRE_34b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_34b), [REQ_TBRE_35a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_35a) |
            | error set next cycle: `assert_TbreErrors_ErrorSetNextCycle` | forward | [REQ_TBRE_32b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_32b), [REQ_TBRE_33a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_33a), [REQ_TBRE_34b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_34b), [REQ_TBRE_35a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_35a) |
            | bad answer raises fault: `assert_TbreErrors_BadAnswerRaisesFault` | forward | [REQ_TBRE_33b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_33b), [REQ_TBRE_34c](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_34c) |
            | RMW fault raises alert: `assert_TbreErrors_RmwFaultRaisesAlert` | forward | [REQ_TBRE_35b](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_35b) |
            | error only for a cause: `assert_TbreErrors_ErrorOnlyForACause` | backward | [REQ_TBRE_36a](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#req_tbre_36a) |

            11 [requirements](../doc/fpv/requirements.md#sweep-errors) belong to this testpoint.'''
      stage: V2S
      priority: "2"
      tests: ["cheriot_mem_sys_fpv"]
      features: ["REQ_TBRE_32a", "REQ_TBRE_32b", "REQ_TBRE_32c", "REQ_TBRE_33a", "REQ_TBRE_33b", "REQ_TBRE_34a", "REQ_TBRE_34b", "REQ_TBRE_34c", "REQ_TBRE_35a", "REQ_TBRE_35b", "REQ_TBRE_36a"]
    }
    {
      name: alert_causes
      desc: '''The alert logic requests the alert only while a fault input of the tag path or of the engine is raised.

